{"id": "19352", "revid": "2253620", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=19352", "title": "Lee's Summit", "text": "Lee's Summit is a city in Missouri. It is the hometown of famous outlaw Cole Younger of the James-Younger Gang, and of Grammy Award-winning musician Pat Metheny.\nUnderstand.\nLee's Summit can provide a family-friendly vacation, and let you get away from the hustle of Kansas City. It encompasses history, shopping, fishing and boating recreation, and relaxation.\nWith great weather; several local festivals; and less crowded stores, restaurants, and attractions, Lee's Summit is a place to visit in the Kansas City metro area. Fall spring and summer are fine times to visit, but avoid the cold and snowy winter here if you can.\nGet in.\nBy train.\nThe town is served by Amtrak with the daily \"Missouri River Runner\", connecting Kansas City with St Louis. is at 220 SW Main St.\nGet around.\nAgain, the best way to get around is by car. So, the major roads in the city are as follows:\nChipman Rd,\n3rd St,\nBlue Pkwy,\nOldham Pkwy,\nDouglas St,\nColbern Rd,\nWard Rd,\nTodd George Rd,\nWoods Chapel Rd,\nThey take you to most places you would visit.\nSee.\nLakes.\nBeaches are open Memorial Day through Labor Day.\nThe arts.\nTo keep up to date on public art displays, check out the Lee's Summit Art Council[dead link] website.\nEat.\nAll Lee's Summit bars and restaurants are completely non-smoking.\nStay safe.\nLee's Summit is one of the safest cities in America, which is a big reason it was ranked the 27th Best Place to Live by CNN/Money Magazine. If you need assistance though call:"}
